{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Your assembly</b> — your congregation, like חית פלשתים (the assembly of the Philistines). And behold, it recounts that Israel entered their land." "And the meaning of תכין — opposite HaShem. Which Israel had in a time of affliction, you prepare for them, that you do good to them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {0 "The lemma חיתך is read as 'your assembly' from חיה in the sense of community; Ibn Ezra draws the analogy to the idiomatic use in 1 Samuel."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:06.118444412Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}